{
  "_about": {
    "purpose": "Vocabulary for ml/ingest.py: what a field report from an Assam oilfield contains that a DeBERTa model pretrained on web English has never seen.",
    "provenance": "Compiled for this project. The abbreviations are standard oil-and-gas and HSE usage; the glossary is common Hindi/Assamese/Bengali safety vocabulary in the romanised spellings that actually appear in typed field reports. It is NOT drawn from a published corpus and it is NOT authoritative.",
    "review_note": "Before this is used on real Oil India reports it must be reviewed and extended by a native Assamese and Hindi speaker who has read the site's own backlog. Romanisation is not standardised -- the same word is typed a dozen ways -- so the `glossary` keys will always be incomplete. This file is meant to be edited by a domain expert without touching any code.",
    "why_english": "The classifier was trained on English narratives only. Devanagari or Bengali script reaches its tokenizer as unknown bytes, and romanised Hindi reaches it as nonsense words. Mapping into English is what lets the model read the report at all -- see docs/RESULTS.md section 5g for what that is worth, measured."
  },

